  "names": {
   "summary": "An 89-byte beacon frame with several multi-byte counters, odd byte-aligned fields that look like parts of larger values, and a few fields correlated with time since an out-of-view eclipse. Many candidate fields are probably misaligned slices of the same counters and flags, so the layout is uncertain.",
   "fields": [
    {
     "offset": 22,
     "name": "uptime_counter",
     "category": "counter",
     "unit": "s",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.4,
     "rationale": "A 3-byte counter rising about 0.117/s with 10 resets in the window, the last one 59.5 days before the end. It wraps within passes, so it is likely a low-rate tick or sequence counter that reboots. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 37,
     "name": "rolling_byte_counter",
     "category": "counter",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.3,
     "rationale": "A 1-byte value that mostly rises and wraps at 255, with 44 resets. It is probably a sequence number or one byte of a larger counter. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 38,
     "name": "misaligned_counter_field",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.15,
     "rationale": "It has a near-zero rate and a median step of 0 but repeats the reset times of offset 22 (60 days before the end). It moves with offsets 45, 51, 52 and 68, so it is likely a misaligned slice of a larger field. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 45,
     "name": "event_counter",
     "category": "counter",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.3,
     "rationale": "A 3-byte counter at about 1.03/s with resets coinciding with offset 22 (59.5 days before the end). It is probably a boot-related counter, and its sun correlation is likely an artefact of when the satellite is heard. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 51,
     "name": "unknown_byte_51",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.133,
     "rationale": "A 1-byte value with only 36 distinct values, moving with the counters. Its lag correlation looks like a time-since-reboot artefact rather than thermal or power physics. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 52,
     "name": "unknown_u16_52",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.117,
     "rationale": "A 16-bit big-endian field with 40 distinct values, tracking the counters and the reboot period. The evidence does not support a physical sensor. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 68,
     "name": "unknown_u32_68",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "counts",
     "scale": "raw * 1",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "Values step in multiples of 2^24, suggesting a misaligned field whose top byte is the only part changing. It follows the same pattern as the other reboot-linked fields. [3/3 samples agree]"
    }
   ],
   "health": "The counters at offsets 22 and 45 reset 10 times in 150 days, the last about 59.5 days before the end, which suggests repeated reboots or counter wraps. The reset count is uncertain because the counters are rolling and may wrap by design. There is not enough evidence on battery or thermal health."
  },
